+# Geometry-derived Partner Closure pilot
+
+Isolated research experiment, based on public Native T1 + Geo at commit `5c11eb2d4a5297612eb77089d3840cb2c1036bde`. It does not alter the default model, the public training loss registry, or official backbone source. No automatic commit, upload or cleanup is performed.
+
+The frozen protocol, checkpoint identities, source references and exact execution records are in `native_t1/runs/geometric_pair_closure_20261001_171356/`. Downloaded reference packages and old assets are read-only. This package must run from the repository root in the existing MeshFlow environment.
+
+Execution is gated and non-resumptive: an existing output folder is an error, not permission to overwrite or repeat training. A failed numerical or matching operation is retained and stops that run. Commands below describe separate authorized stages, not an instruction to rerun a completed experiment.
+
+```bash
+python -B -m experiments.mf_h1_local0.geometric_pair_closure_pilot.capture --out RUN
+python -B -m experiments.mf_h1_local0.geometric_pair_closure_pilot.diagnose --out RUN
+python -B -m experiments.mf_h1_local0.geometric_pair_closure_pilot.calibrate --out RUN
+python -B -m experiments.mf_h1_local0.geometric_pair_closure_pilot.train --out RUN --arm P_Time
+python -B -m experiments.mf_h1_local0.geometric_pair_closure_pilot.train --out RUN --arm P_Conf
+python -B -m experiments.mf_h1_local0.geometric_pair_closure_pilot.final_sampling --out RUN
+python -B -m experiments.mf_h1_local0.geometric_pair_closure_pilot.post --out RUN
+```
+
+Asset and GT compatibility audits and CPU fixtures precede `capture`; they are not bypassed by the commands. Formal training requires a complete 48-state teacher grid, an admissible time window and a calibration cryptographically bound to that window. Pair uses detached current endpoint geometry for general-graph minimum-weight perfect matching, then differentiates FP32 endpoint distances with frozen partners and weights. It never reads GT connectivity or GT bbox. Original FM and finite-edge supervision remain supervised. Confidence masks retain the full matching denominator.
+
+Each arm uses 500 fresh-AdamW updates from the same G0_2500 state and restored historical input stream. Pair applies to one independently registered sample per effective batch, without a second division by eight. `train.py` has a private strict checkpoint schema; these experimental losses do not impersonate a public FM or JEdge5 recipe.
+
+The four frozen models are evaluated on 160 registered 50-step rollouts. All raw arrays are saved before the common postprocessing stage. Stage 2 constructs one candidate using full matching, C-protected endpoint equivalence classes and equal-weight free-coordinate means. It does not retry, delete faces or repair holes. C conflicts are explicit failures. A constructed candidate is not a legality certificate.
+
+`evaluation.py` separates raw coordinate topology, explicit candidate topology and floating-point dual intersection audits. The GT is used only for scoring and displacement normalization. Failed construction and unresolved audit requests remain in the denominator of effective closure rates. This is not exact-predicate certification.
+
+`aggregate.py` and `figures.py` only consume saved outputs; they do not rerun the model, matcher or geometric scorer. The final report distinguishes teacher correspondence, unconstrained free generation, training effects and postprocessing effects.
+
+CPU fixture sources are under `tests/` plus `test_capture.py`. Historical execution records distinguish genuine model calls from mocked objective assemblies and small tensor autograd fixtures. No fixture performs an optimizer update on the real generator.
